window.docContents[110].resolve({"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L3-___-The-body-opens-up--Synopsis--PKC-vocabulary-in-scope":{"contents":"New at this step:\n\n* WeightedCarving (parts, weight, mean, total_ne_zero) — a carving with per-part weights whose mean requires nonzero total weight.* totalWeight, weightedSum — the pieces of a weighted mean.* Decomposition.fold — a value per part, combined over a decomposition.* InFrame — components read in a stated frame.* union_mass, union_centerOfMass, union_inertiaTensor — how mass, centre of mass and inertia combine over a union.* labOmega, bodyOmega, bodyInertia, rotationalContraction — rigid-body quantities indexed by frame.\n\nCarried from earlier steps: Composite, Decomposition, Assembles, assemble, IndividualQuantity, DifferenceKind.ofScale, SortOfSystem, Sorted, Designated, displacementK.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L3 — The body opens up\u0009Synopsis","header":"5.4.1.2. PKC vocabulary in scope","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L3-___-The-body-opens-up--Synopsis--PKC-vocabulary-in-scope"},"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L5-___-The-oscillation-dies-out--Questions-to-ask-the-model-so-far":{"contents":"* Question* Check* What the verdict means\n* Does the damper conserve mechanical energy?* energy_dissipation* No; with positive γ and nonzero velocity, the energy derivative is negative.\n* What does γ measure?* kinds_and_decay_rate* The viscous damping constant measured on the damper, not the ISO whole-system damping coefficient.\n* Can A's γ be divided by B's mass?* kinds_and_decay_rate* No; the quotient requires both quantities to share the same oscillator bearer.\n* What is δ?* kinds_and_decay_rate* PhysLib's decayRate, carried on the named whole and kinded as ISO 3-24 damping coefficient.\n* Can δ be added to ω₀?* same_dimension_different_kinds* Not as kinded quantities: both have dimension T⁻¹, but they are different kinds.\n* How is underdamping tested?* underdamped_regime* Compare magnitudes explicitly; the physical criterion is the dimensionless ratio δ/ω₀ < 1.\n* Can the damper-aging state be compared with another state of A?* same_oscillator_states* Yes; the typed change reads the later and earlier state fields.\n* Can A's δ be mixed with B's?* same_oscillator_states* No; distinct nominal names are distinct systems.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L5 — The oscillation dies out","header":"5.6.9. Questions to ask the model so far","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L5-___-The-oscillation-dies-out--Questions-to-ask-the-model-so-far"},"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L5-___-The-oscillation-dies-out--Synopsis":{"contents":"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L5 — The oscillation dies out","header":"5.6.1. Synopsis","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L5-___-The-oscillation-dies-out--Synopsis"}});